# A worker runs the program once more in a VM of its own, and no object crosses over. So the program that starts one has one instance in its VM, with evaluated text or without,
# and an object that passes a test for its layout needs no test for its instance.
# FORM: AsRead
# RUN: valueflow-results
# CHECK: unseen-code EvaluatesText
# CHECK: program instances AtMostOne

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="input" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Builtin builtin=Function
    v3 = Construct v2, -, v1
    v4 = Call v3
    v5 = Builtin builtin=Worker
    v6 = Construct v5, -, v1
    Return
}
